      'An Italian meal comes in courses: **l’antipasto** (starter), **il primo** (pasta, rice or soup), **il secondo** (meat or fish) and **il dolce** (dessert). You do not have to order them all. To ask for a table say **Un tavolo per due, per favore.** The waiter asks **Che cosa prende?** (formal). **C’è** means “there is” and **ci sono** “there are”: **C’è un menù in inglese?** **Ci sono due tavoli liberi.** After **per** and **di** a pronoun or noun follows without a change; **la** goes before the dish you pick: **Prendo la pizza.**',
