      'To say where you live use **abitare in** with a type of home (**in un appartamento**, **in una casa**). A house or flat **ha** (has) rooms and a garden: **La casa ha un giardino grande.** Italian puts the adjective after the noun: **un appartamento piccolo**. Many plural nouns follow the -o → -i, -a → -e pattern: **gatto** → **gatti**, **cane** → **cani**, **pesce** → **pesci**. **non** goes before the verb: **Non ho animali.** Pets usually have names: **Il mio gatto si chiama Leo.**',
