      'Say how you travel with **in** and the vehicle: **in treno**, **in autobus**, **in macchina**. On foot is **a piedi**. Buy a ticket with **Un biglietto per Roma, per favore.** The train leaves **dal binario due** (“from platform two”). **partire** (to leave) is an -ire verb: **parto**, **parti**, **parte**, **partiamo**, **partite**, **partono**. **arrivare** (to arrive) is an -are verb: **arriva**. **vicino** is “near” and **lontano** “far”. **La stazione è vicina** uses **vicina** because stazione is feminine.',
